  data: {
    LLM: "Play starts with the highest double (12-12) in the center. Each player has a personal train from the hub; a shared Mexican Train is open to all. On the first turn only, a player may play as many matching tiles as they can on their train. From the second turn onward, each player plays one tile per turn (or more if playing doubles) onto their own train, another player's marked train, or the Mexican Train. If unable to play, the player draws one tile from the boneyard and may play it if it fits; otherwise they pass and place a marker on their train. Exposed doubles must be satisfied by the next player. The first player to play all tiles wins the round; otherwise the player with fewest pips in hand wins when blocked.",
    Player: "Play starts with the highest double (12-12) in the center. Each player has a personal train from the hub; a shared Mexican Train is open to all. On the first turn only, a player may play as many matching tiles as they can on their train. From the second turn onward, each player plays one tile per turn (or more if playing doubles) onto their own train, another player's marked train, or the Mexican Train. If unable to play, the player draws one tile from the boneyard and may play it if it fits; otherwise they pass and place a marker on their train. Exposed doubles must be satisfied by the next player. The first player to play all tiles wins the round; otherwise the player with fewest pips in hand wins when blocked.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to play all your dominoes, or have the lowest pip count when the game is blocked.',
    gameplay: "Play starts with the highest double (12-12) in the center. Each player has a personal train from the hub; a shared Mexican Train is open to all. On the first turn only, a player may play as many matching tiles as they can on their train. From the second turn onward, each player plays one tile per turn (or more if playing doubles) onto their own train, another player's marked train, or the Mexican Train. If unable to play, the player draws one tile from the boneyard and may play it if it fits; otherwise they pass and place a marker on their train. Exposed doubles must be satisfied by the next player. The first player to play all tiles wins the round; otherwise the player with fewest pips in hand wins when blocked.",
